00:06:10.180 --> 00:06:13.470
We started doing OpenStack
and then, about a year ago,

00:06:13.470 --> 00:06:15.570
started working with
Kubernetes as well.

00:06:15.570 --> 00:06:19.290
And I worked for
a while at VMware.

00:06:19.290 --> 00:06:22.500
That's how I know some of the
people who started the company.

00:06:22.500 --> 00:06:26.130
And I had worked on
various things at VMware--

00:06:26.130 --> 00:06:30.240
infrastructure management
stuff, some storage systems,

00:06:30.240 --> 00:06:33.640
and some other random
projects in between.

00:06:33.640 --> 00:06:36.630
And so that's why I joined
here and was working

00:06:36.630 --> 00:06:39.270
on this Kubernetes
management plane

00:06:39.270 --> 00:06:41.580
and then maybe about
four to six months ago

00:06:41.580 --> 00:06:42.880
started working on Fission.

00:06:42.880 --> 00:06:43.630
MARK MANDEL: Cool.

00:06:43.630 --> 00:06:45.280
And what is your
role on Fission?

00:06:45.280 --> 00:06:47.970
SOAM VASANI: So I'm the
software engineer on it.

00:06:47.970 --> 00:06:51.640
It's actually mainly just
one person right now.

00:06:51.640 --> 00:06:54.639
So I guess I'm software engineer
